<DocsLayout title="Shell Patterns" description="60+ shell compression patterns that reduce command output tokens by 70-90%.">
  <h1>Shell Compression Patterns</h1>
  <p>lean-ctx includes 60+ compression modules that intelligently reduce shell command output before it reaches your AI. Patterns are applied automatically when using <code>lean-ctx -c "command"</code> or the shell hook.</p>

  <h2>How It Works</h2>
  <p>When your AI runs a command through lean-ctx:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>The command executes normally</li>
    <li>lean-ctx matches output against its pattern library</li>
    <li>Matched patterns compress the output (removing noise, keeping signal)</li>
    <li>Compressed output is delivered to the AI</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Pattern Categories</h2>

  <h3>Git (12 patterns)</h3>
  <p>Compresses git status, log, diff, blame, branch, stash, and more. Removes unchanged listings, compresses headers, keeps only meaningful diff content.</p>
  <pre><code># git status: 80% reduction
# Removes "nothing to commit" boilerplate, compresses file lists

# git log: 75% reduction
# Keeps commit hash + message, removes author/date noise

# git diff: 70% reduction
# Compresses context lines, keeps only +/- lines</code></pre>

  <h3>Build Tools (15 patterns)</h3>
  <p>cargo, npm, pip, go build, make — strips compilation progress, keeps only errors and final status.</p>
  <pre><code># cargo build: 90% reduction
# "Compiling crate 1/47..." lines removed, errors preserved

# npm install: 85% reduction
# Progress bars and "added X packages" noise removed</code></pre>

  <h3>Test Runners (10 patterns)</h3>
  <p>cargo test, pytest, jest, go test — removes passing test output, highlights failures.</p>
  <pre><code># cargo test: 90% reduction
# 200 "test result: ok" lines → "47 passed, 0 failed"

# pytest: 85% reduction
# Collection output removed, only failures + summary kept</code></pre>

  <h3>File System (8 patterns)</h3>
  <p>ls, find, tree, du — tabular compression, removes metadata noise.</p>

  <h3>System / Process (10 patterns)</h3>
  <p>ps, top, docker, systemctl — keeps running processes, removes formatting.</p>

  <h3>Network (5 patterns)</h3>
  <p>curl headers, wget output, ping — removes progress, keeps response data.</p>

  <h2>Savings Overview</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Avg Savings</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Git</td><td>70-80%</td><td>git status, git log, git diff</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Build</td><td>85-95%</td><td>cargo build, npm install</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Test</td><td>85-95%</td><td>cargo test, pytest, jest</td></tr>
      <tr><td>File System</td><td>70-80%</td><td>ls, find, tree</td></tr>
      <tr><td>System</td><td>60-75%</td><td>ps, docker ps</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Custom Patterns</h2>
  <p>Add custom patterns in <code>~/.config/lean-ctx/patterns/</code>. Each pattern is a TOML file defining match conditions and compression rules.</p>
